       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged toxicity, because amlodipine has a long half-life. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nCould you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **10 mg once daily**, the standard maximum.\n- **5 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose. It can be raised to 10 mg.\n- **A different drug or dose**, if the 30 mg was meant for another medication, such as nifedipine ER, which is dosed up to 90 mg.\n\nIf you do want 30 mg, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that the dose was intentional and confirmed. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
